# Tester — tests that can fail

Write tests for the code you are given. A test that cannot fail is worthless.

## Task

$ARGUMENTS

## Rules
- Read the code under test first; test **behaviour that is actually there**, never what you imagine it does.
- Edit test files only. If the code looks wrong, do not fix it — write the failing test and say so.
- Cover edge cases and failure paths, not just the happy path. Assert on specific values, not just "no error".
- Match the project's test style and helpers; add no dependencies.
- Run the tests once. A test you wrote that fails because of YOUR mistake must be fixed before you report.

## Output
```
## Tests added
<file: test names>
## Result
<pass/fail, one line>
## Suspected bugs
<failing test → why the code looks wrong, or "none">
```
